# File Creation Rules
- Generate complete, standalone files when creating new code.
- Include imports, interfaces, and implementation in the same file unless modularized elsewhere.
- Don't forget JSDoc (in english) with proper typing, return values and examples when it could be handy
- Add `"use client"` only when the file uses state, effects, context or event wiring (see `architecture.mdc`).
- Never import the stylesheet from a component: users import `magic-pill/styles.css` once. Style with `data-mp` attributes, not class names.
- Example structure for a new template file (a stateless arrangement of the pill's parts, so no `"use client"`):
```tsx
import type { ReactNode } from "react";

import { PillActions, PillDivider, PillIcon, PillMessage } from "../Pill/parts";
import PillAction from "../Pill/PillAction";

export interface PillPromptProps {
  icon?: ReactNode;
  /** Any content. Never parsed as HTML. */
  question: ReactNode;
  /** The answer button's label, e.g. "Yes". */
  answerLabel: string;
  onAnswer: () => void;
}

/**
 * A question with a single answer, e.g. "Do you need some help?" · ✓ Yes.
 * Render it inside a <Pill>.
 *
 * @example
 * <Pill><PillPrompt icon={<HelpIcon />} question="Do you need some help?" answerLabel="Yes" onAnswer={openHelp} /></Pill>
 */
export function PillPrompt({ icon, question, answerLabel, onAnswer }: PillPromptProps) {
  return (
    <>
      {icon && (
        <>
          <PillIcon>{icon}</PillIcon>
          <PillDivider />
        </>
      )}
      <PillMessage>{question}</PillMessage>
      <PillActions>
        <PillAction label={answerLabel} onClick={onAnswer} />
      </PillActions>
    </>
  );
}
```
